    "sections": [
      {
        "id": "about",
        "heading": "About Mercury Auto Transport",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Mercury Auto Transport is a licensed auto transport broker matching shippers with vetted carrier networks. The company positions itself on transparent pricing and a broad national footprint, with emphasis on major corridors and repeat-shipper relationships."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "how-it-works",
        "heading": "How it works",
        "paragraphs": [
          "You book a window and provide vehicle details; Mercury sources capacity from its network and assigns a carrier. Pricing is typically locked or refined once a carrier is assigned, and contracts spell out insurance and pickup or delivery terms before dispatch."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "pricing",
        "heading": "Pricing — what “93% accuracy” actually means",
        "paragraphs": [
          "The headline accuracy figure reflects how often final invoices stay within a narrow band of the initial quote. Market fuel changes, last-minute date shifts, and rural access can still move price—those events are the usual exceptions, not a hidden fee structure if disclosed up front in your quote pack."
        ],
        "callout": {
          "label": "Pricing ranges:",
          "lines": [
            "Short-haul (under 500 mi): often mid–high three figures on open transport.",
            "Cross-country: commonly low four figures open; enclosed adds a meaningful premium on most lanes.",
            "Expedited and enclosed luxury moves: priced case-by-case with carrier-availability constraints."
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "carrier-network",
        "heading": "Carrier network",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Mercury is strongest where carrier density is high—e.g. state-to-state trunk routes and large metros. In rural pickup or drop-off scenarios, expect fewer carrier options, longer lead times, or higher all-in cost; condition scores in those lanes are still tracked but with less schedule slack."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "communication",
        "heading": "Communication — the honest picture",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Most shipments receive timely booking and pickup confirmation. On long-haul transits, a minority of customers report lulls in proactive updates; getting direct contact from the driver at pickup mitigates that gap. Resolution timelines vary when things go off-script—set expectations from your BOL and carrier handoff."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "best-for",
        "heading": "Who Mercury is best for — and when to look elsewhere",
        "paragraphs": [],
        "labeledBlocks": [
          {
            "label": "Best for:",
            "text": "Planned moves on well-traveled lanes, customers who can book 7–14 days out, and shippers who value quote clarity and a single point of contact through dispatch."
          },
          {
            "label": "Consider alternatives if:",
            "text": "You need same-week rural pickup, guaranteed enclosed specialists for exotic vehicles, or a marketplace with live carrier bidding in real time—those profiles may get more flexibility from other models."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
